come was binarized (any red card vs none)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[126, 126]], "assertion": "the exposure was binarized at the 0.75 threshold (very dark vs very light)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exposure variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[127, 127]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[128, 128]], "note": "Software sub-label"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[129, 129]], "assertion": "Python 3.9+, pandas 1.5+, numpy 1.23+, statsmodels 0.14+, and scipy 1.9+ were used", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["software"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[130, 130]], "assertion": "a random seed of 42 was set for reproducibility", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["random seed"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[131, 131]], "assertion": "complete reproducible code was provided in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["code"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[132, 134]], "note": "blank, separator, blank"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[135, 136]], "note": "## 4. CONCLUSION heading and blank line"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[137, 138]], "assertion": "the overall conclusion is labeled SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 121, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[139, 140]], "note": "lead-in sentence framing the evidence summary, plus blank line"}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[141, 141]], "note": "Evidence Summary sub-label"}, {"id": 